    dmo:onsetPattern "Chronic" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with diabetes and chronic kidney disease (CKD) should be treated with a comprehensive strategy to reduce risks of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Moderately or severely increased albuminuria is related to increased kidney and cardiovascular risk compared to normal albumin excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "50% of patients had established CVD" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Primary outcome Kidney composite: kidney failure, a sustained decrease ≥40% in GFR, renal death CV composite: death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, nonfatal stroke, or hospitalization for HF" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with diabetes and CKD often have other chronic comorbidities, including obesity, that contribute to the higher risk of CVD and kidney disease progression." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

