<https://example.org/dmo/id/diabetesType/type-1-diabetes> a dmo:DiabetesType ;
    rdfs:label "Type 1 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:definition "Type 1 Diabetes (T1D) is an autoimmune condition characterized by the destruction of pancreatic beta cells, leading to absolute insulin deficiency." ;
    dmo:diabetesTypeCode "type-1-diabetes" ;
    dmo:insulinRequired "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    dmo:mondoCode "MONDO:0005147" ;
    dmo:name "Type 1 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:prevalenceShare "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    dmo:typicalOnset "Childhood" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Table S60. SoF table: T1D and CKD (G1 –G2)—intensive insulin versus conventional insulin" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Type 1 diabetes (T1D) and T2D are both addressed, with differences in approach to management highlighted when appropriate." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Glycemic control is based on insulin for type 1 diabetes (T1D)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Recommendation 1.3.1: We recommend treating patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D), CKD, and an eGFR ‡20 ml/min per 1.73 m 2 with an SGLT2i (1A)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "T1D, type 1 diabetes; T2D, type 2 diabetes." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to patients with either T1D and T2D, as well as kidney transplant recipients; however, this recommendation does not apply to patients on dialysis." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to patients with T1D or T2D." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "CGM metrics such as time in range and time in hypoglycemia have been studied most often among patients with T1D, who tend to have greater glycemic variability than patients with T2D and are at higher risk of hypoglycemia ( Figure 12 )." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to both T1D and T2D, as well as kidney transplant recipients, but not to dialysis patients (see Practice Point 3.1.2)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Future studies should focus on kidney and heart protective benefits of GLP-1 RA, as well as their safety, for use in patients with T1D." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Population Adults with CKD (G1 –G5, G5D) and diabetes (T1D and T2D)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "She was diagnosed with type 1 diabetes at the age of 13" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "effects of enalapril and losartan in type 1 diabetes. N Engl J Med . 2009;361:40 –51." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/diabetesType/type-2-diabetes> a dmo:DiabetesType ;
    rdfs:label "Type 2 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:definition "Type 2 Diabetes (T2D) is characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, typically developing in adults, especially with obesity and sedentary lifestyle." ;
    dmo:diabetesTypeCode "type-2-diabetes" ;
    dmo:insulinRequired "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    dmo:mondoCode "MONDO:0005148" ;
    dmo:name "Type 2 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:prevalenceShare "0.9"^^xsd:decimal ;
    dmo:typicalOnset "Adulthood" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Table S61. SoF table: T2D and CKD (G1 –G2)—insulin degludec versus insulin glargine" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Chapter 4: Glucose-lowering therapies in patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D) and CKD." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Type 1 diabetes (T1D) and T2D are both addressed, with differences in approach to management highlighted when appropriate." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Glycemic control is based on insulin for type 1 diabetes (T1D) and a combination of metformin and sodium –glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitors (SGLT2i) for type 2 diabetes (T2D)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Recommendation 1.3.1: We recommend treating patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D), CKD, and an eGFR ‡20 ml/min per 1.73 m 2 with an SGLT2i (1A)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For patients with T2D and CKD who choose not to do daily glycemic monitoring by CGM or SMBG, glucose-lowering agents that pose a lower risk of hypoglycemia are preferred and should be administered in doses that are appropriate for the level of eGFR." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "We recommend treating patients with T2D, CKD, and an eGFR ‡30 ml/min per 1.73 m 2 with metformin (1B)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to patients with either T1D and T2D, as well as kidney transplant recipients; however, this recommendation does not apply to patients on dialysis." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Although the IDNT 13 and IRMA-2 11 studies recruited exclusively patients with T2D and hypertension" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with T2D and CKD are at increased risk of both cardiovascular events and progression to kidney failure." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "T2D (with an HbA1c level of 6.5% –12.0%) and CKD, defined by an eGFR of 30 –90 ml/min per 1.73 m 2 with albuminuria (ACR of 300 –5000 mg/g [30 –500 mg/mmol])" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "those with T2D and albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to patients with T1D or T2D." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with diabetes and more advanced CKD stages are at increased risk of hypoglycemia." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "HbA1c targets #6.0% were associated with greater risk of hypoglycemia and increased mortality in patients with T2D and increased cardiovascular risk." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to both T1D and T2D, as well as kidney transplant recipients, but not to dialysis patients (see Practice Point 3.1.2)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Practice Point 4.1: Glycemic management for patients with T2D and CKD should include lifestyle therapy, first-line treatment with both metformin and a sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor (SGLT2i), and additional drug therapy as needed for glycemic control ( Figure 23 )." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For patients with T2D, CKD, and an eGFR $30 ml/min per 1.73 m 2 not currently treated with glucose-lowering drugs" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "diabetes (T2D) and chronic kidney disease (CKD)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "blind RCT of adults with T2D who were randomly assigned to 1 of 3 extended-release metformin treatment regimens" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The Peptide Innovation for Early Diabetes Treatment (PIONEER) 6 study investigated the cardiovascular safety of an oral GLP-1 RA (oral semaglutide). 383 The study evaluated 3183 patients with T2D and high cardiovascular risk, CKD, or age >50 years with a major CVD risk factor." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "in patients with diabetes and CKD conducted by the ERT" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with T2D and CKD bene ﬁted from GLP-1 RA therapy in RCTs." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Both of these team-based care models in patients with T2D and CKD focusing on treatment with multiple targets and self-management were found to be cost-effective and cost-saving, if implemented in the primary care setting." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Population Adults with CKD (G1 –G5, G5D) and diabetes (T1D and T2D)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "type 2 diabetes mellitus, established cardiovascular disease, and chronic kidney disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "patients with type 2 diabetes and chronic kidney disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "391. Davies MJ, Bain SC, Atkin SL, et al. Ef ﬁcacy and safety of liraglutide versus placebo as add-on to glucose-lowering therapy in patients with type 2 diabetes and moderate renal impairment (LIRA-RENAL): a randomized clinical trial. Diabetes Care . 2016;39:222 –230." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/diabetesType/type-2-diabetic-patients> a dmo:DiabetesType ;
    rdfs:label "Type 2 Diabetic Patients" ;
    dmo:definition "Type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) is characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, typically developing in adulthood." ;
    dmo:diabetesTypeCode "type-2-diabetic-patients" ;
