    dmo:evidenceQuote "A nonsteroidal mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist (ns-MRA) can be added to ﬁrst-line therapy for patients with T2D and high residual risks of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular events, as evidenced by persistent albuminuria ( >30 mg/g [ >3 mg/mmol])." ;
