<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-nonsteroidal-mineralocorticoid-receptor-antagonist-ns-mra-in-t2d-with-high-residual-risk> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of nonsteroidal mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist (ns-MRA) in T2D with high residual risk" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D) and chronic kidney disease (CKD) with high residual risk of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular events" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-nonsteroidal-mineralocorticoid-receptor-antagonist-ns-mra-in-t2d-with-high-residual-risk" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "A nonsteroidal mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist (ns-MRA) can be added to first-line therapy for patients with T2D and high residual risks of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular events, as evidenced by persistent albuminuria ( >30 mg/g [ >3 mg/mmol])" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A nonsteroidal mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist (ns-MRA) can be added to first-line therapy for patients with T2D and high residual risks of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular events, as evidenced by persistent albuminuria ( >30 mg/g [ >3 mg/mmol])" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-nonsteroidal-mra-in-patients-with-lower-levels-of-albuminuria> a dmo:Recommendation ;
