<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/acute-kidney-injury> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Acute Kidney Injury" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The use of steroidal MRA increases the risk of acute kidney injury (by 2-fold)" ;
    dmo:name "Acute Kidney Injury" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "acute-kidney-injury" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Further, the use of steroidal MRA also increases the risk of hyperkalemia (by 2–3 fold) and acute kidney injury (by 2-fold)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/advanced-age> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Advanced Age" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是高钾血症的风险因素" ;
    dmo:name "Advanced Age" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "advanced-age" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors for the development of hyperkalemia with the use of drugs that inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "at inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/advanced-chronic-kidney-disease-ckd> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Advanced Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Advanced CKD substantially increases the risk of hypoglycemia in patients with diabetes treated by many oral agents and insulin." ;
    dmo:name "Advanced Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "advanced-chronic-kidney-disease-ckd" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Advanced CKD substantially increases the risk of hypoglycemia in patients with diabetes treated by many oral agents and insulin." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/advanced-ckd> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Advanced CKD" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Patients with diabetes and more advanced CKD stages are at increased risk of hypoglycemia." ;
    dmo:name "Advanced CKD" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "advanced-ckd" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with diabetes and more advanced CKD stages are at increased risk of hypoglycemia." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with advanced CKD may naturally decrease their oral intake, leading to malnutrition." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/aggressive-diuretic-use> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Aggressive Diuretic Use" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是使用RAS阻断剂后血清肌酐急性升高的潜在原因" ;
    dmo:name "Aggressive Diuretic Use" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "aggressive-diuretic-use" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "which often occurs in the setting of volume depletion with aggressive diuretic use and low cardiac output seen in heart failure, or with the use of nonsteroidal anti-in ﬂammatory drugs." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/albuminuria> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Albuminuria is a marker of kidney damage and is targeted with RAS blockade and ns-MRA, indicating it is a modifiable risk factor." ;
    dmo:name "Albuminuria" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A nonsteroidal mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist (ns-MRA) can be added to first-line therapy for patients with T2D and high residual risks of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular events, as evidenced by persistent albuminuria ( >30 mg/g [ >3 mg/mmol])." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "albuminuria, and normal blood pressure" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Recently, 2 large clinical trials have examined the cardiovascular and kidney effects of finerenone in those with T2D and albuminuria" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/anemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Anemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Anemia is associated with shortened survival or age of erythrocytes, which lowers HbA1c levels, reducing its reliability as a glycemic marker in advanced CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Anemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "anemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Conversely, HbA1c is lowered by shortened survival or age of erythrocytes from anemia, transfusions, and use of erythropoiesis-stimulating agents or iron-replacement therapies." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Further, loss of muscle mass and development of complications such as anemia might limit the functional capacity of these patients as kidney function continues to decline." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/bilateral-renal-artery-stenosis> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Bilateral Renal Artery Stenosis" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是使用RAS阻断剂后血清肌酐急性升高的潜在原因" ;
    dmo:name "Bilateral Renal Artery Stenosis" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "bilateral-renal-artery-stenosis" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "bilateral renal artery stenosis (or stenosis of a single renal artery for patients with a single functioning kidney, including kidney transplant recipients) might also be a cause of elevated serum creatinine following initiation of RAS blockade treatment" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/chronic-kidney-disease> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Chronic Kidney Disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是使用ACEi或ARB治疗的适应症，但也是高钾血症的风险因素" ;
    dmo:name "Chronic Kidney Disease" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "chronic-kidney-disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors for the development of hyperkalemia with the use of drugs that inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/ckd> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "CKD" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "CKD is listed as a risk factor for hyperkalemia in the context of RAS inhibition." ;
    dmo:name "CKD" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "ckd" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "at inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/concurrent-diuretic-use> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent diuretic use" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document explicitly identifies concurrent diuretic use as a risk factor for volume depletion in the context of SGLT2 inhibitor initiation." ;
    dmo:name "Concurrent diuretic use" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "concurrent-diuretic-use" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Volume depletion risk?  Concurrent diuretic use" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote " Concurrent diuretic use" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/constipation> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "constipation" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Constipation is a risk factor for hyperkalemia and should be avoided through sufficient fluid intake and exercise." ;
    dmo:name "constipation" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "constipation" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "General measures to avoid constipation should include sufﬁcient ﬂuid intake and exercise." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/decompensated-congestive-heart-failure> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Decompensated Congestive Heart Failure" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是高钾血症的风险因素，可通过治疗管理" ;
    dmo:name "Decompensated Congestive Heart Failure" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "decompensated-congestive-heart-failure" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors for the development of hyperkalemia with the use of drugs that inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "at inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/diabetes> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Diabetes is a primary condition that increases risk of CKD and cardiovascular disease." ;
    dmo:name "Diabetes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with diabetes and chronic kidney disease (CKD) should be treated with a comprehensive strategy to reduce risks of kidney disease progression and cardiovascular disease ( Figures 1 and 2)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This recommendation applies to patients with T1D or T2D." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors for the development of hyperkalemia with the use of drugs that inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "at inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/dyslipidemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Dyslipidemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Dyslipidemia is a modifiable risk factor for cardiovascular disease progression in patients with diabetes and CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Dyslipidemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "dyslipidemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A statin is recommended for all patients with T1D or T2D and CKD." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/emotional-distress> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional Distress" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档中提到在T2D患者中，特别是那些有社会差异或情绪困扰的患者，心理社会支持可以改善代谢控制和情绪健康。" ;
    dmo:name "Emotional Distress" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "emotional-distress" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In some patients with T2D, especially those with social disparity or emotional distress, psychosocial support from peers 443 and community healthcare workers444 can also improve metabolic control and emotional well-being, and reduce hospitalizations." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/erythropoiesis-stimulating-agents> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Erythropoiesis-Stimulating Agents" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Use of erythropoiesis-stimulating agents contributes to shortened survival or age of erythrocytes, which lowers HbA1c levels, reducing its reliability as a glycemic marker in advanced CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Erythropoiesis-Stimulating Agents" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "erythropoiesis-stimulating-agents" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Conversely, HbA1c is lowered by shortened survival or age of erythrocytes from anemia, transfusions, and use of erythropoiesis-stimulating agents or iron-replacement therapies." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/established-cardiovascular-disease> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Established Cardiovascular Disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document states that 89.6% of participants in the efpeglenatide trial had established CVD." ;
    dmo:name "Established Cardiovascular Disease" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "established-cardiovascular-disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "including 89.6% with established CVD." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/extensive-ascvd> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Extensive ASCVD" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是使用RAS阻断剂后血清肌酐急性升高的潜在原因" ;
    dmo:name "Extensive ASCVD" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "extensive-ascvd" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "especially in patients with extensive ASCVD or who are smokers." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/genital-infection-risk> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Genital infection risk" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document explicitly lists genital infection risk as a potential contraindication to SGLT2 inhibitor use." ;
    dmo:name "Genital infection risk" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "genital-infection-risk" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Potential contraindications:  Genital infection risk" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote " Genital infection risk" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/genital-mycotic-infections> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Genital Mycotic Infections" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The increased risk of genital mycotic infections with SGL T2i treatment in both men and women that is consistent across all trials." ;
    dmo:name "Genital Mycotic Infections" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "genital-mycotic-infections" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There is an increased risk of genital mycotic infections with SGL T2i treatment in both men and women that is consistent across all trials." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hba1c-9-5> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "HbA1c ≤9.5%" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document states that the REWIND trial included adults with T2D with HbA1c of #9.5% (with no lower limit)." ;
    dmo:name "HbA1c ≤9.5%" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "hba1c-9-5" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The REWIND trial (evaluating dulaglutide) included 9901 adults with T2D with HbA1c of #9.5% (with no lower limit and mean HbA1c of 7.2%)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/high-residual-risk-of-ckd-progression-and-cardiovascular-events> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "High Residual Risk of CKD Progression and Cardiovascular Events" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Patients with T2D and albuminuria are known to be at high risk of CKD progression and cardiovascular events, and finerenone reduced these events among such patients." ;
    dmo:name "High Residual Risk of CKD Progression and Cardiovascular Events" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "high-residual-risk-of-ckd-progression-and-cardiovascular-events" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with T2D and albuminuria are known to be at high risk of CKD progression and cardiovascular events, and the FIDELIO-DKD and FIGARO-DKD trials demonstrated that finerenone reduced these events (particularly CKD progression and heart failure) among such patients." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/high-risk-of-atherosclerotic-cardiovascular-disease-ascvd> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "High Risk of Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease (ASCVD)" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Aspirin may be considered for primary prevention among patients with high risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD)." ;
    dmo:name "High Risk of Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease (ASCVD)" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "high-risk-of-atherosclerotic-cardiovascular-disease-ascvd" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Aspirin generally should be used lifelong for secondary prevention among those with established cardiovascular disease and may be considered for primary prevention among patients with high risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/high-sodium-intake> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "High Sodium Intake" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Sodium intake should be <2 g of sodium per day (or <90 mmol of sodium per day, or <5 g of sodium chloride per day) in patients with diabetes and CKD." ;
    dmo:name "High Sodium Intake" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "high-sodium-intake" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "We suggest that sodium intake be <2 g of sodium per day (or <90 mmol of sodium per day, or <5 g of sodium chloride per day) in patients with diabetes and CKD (2C)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Using the lowest levels of sodium intake from RCTs and evidence from the best-designed balance study conducted among adults, which used neutral balance with heat stress at 1525 mg/day, as well as utilizing data from the DASH Sodium Trial and eight other RCTs, assessment was made that the sodium recommendations were congruent and appropriate to recommend 1500 mg/day for all age groups 14 and over. For those with intakes above 2300 mg, the recommendation is to decrease intake." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "High sodium intake increases blood pressure and risk of kidney disease. From the Science of Salt: a regularly updated systematic review of salt and health outcomes (August 2016 to March 2017)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/history-of-severe-hypoglycemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "History of severe hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document explicitly lists history of severe hypoglycemia as a factor to consider when assessing hypoglycemia risk with SGLT2 inhibitors." ;
    dmo:name "History of severe hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "history-of-severe-hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Hypoglycemia risk?  Insulin or sulfonylurea  History of severe hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote " History of severe hypoglycemia" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/history-of-urinary-tract-infections> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "History of Urinary Tract Infections" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "People with a history of urinary tract infections also may not prefer this class of medications." ;
    dmo:name "History of Urinary Tract Infections" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "history-of-urinary-tract-infections" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People with a history of urinary tract infections also may not prefer this class of medications." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hyperglycemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Hyperglycemia is a modifiable risk factor for microvascular and macrovascular complications in diabetes, including progression of CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Hyperglycemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "hyperglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Glycemic control is based on insulin for type 1 diabetes (T1D) and a combination of metformin and sodium –glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitors (SGLT2i) for type 2 diabetes (T2D)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "These risks are mediated by “indirect” effects such as worsened risk factors (e.g., hyperglycemia, hypertension) as well as by “direct” effects of obesity (e.g., pro-in ﬂammatory state, fat compression of organs)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hyperkalemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperkalemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "与使用ACEi或ARB相关，可管理" ;
    dmo:name "Hyperkalemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "hyperkalemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Hyperkalemia is a known complication with RAS blockade and occurs in up to 10% of outpatients" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Further, the use of steroidal MRA also increases the risk of hyperkalemia (by 2–3 fold) and acute kidney injury (by 2-fold)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hyperlipidemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperlipidemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Hyperlipidemia is addressed through statin therapy, which is recommended for all patients with T1D or T2D and CKD, indicating it is a modifiable risk factor." ;
    dmo:name "Hyperlipidemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "hyperlipidemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A statin is recommended for all patients with T1D or T2D and CKD." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hypertension> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Hypertension" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Hypertension is explicitly mentioned as a target for intervention with RAS blockade, indicating it is a modifiable risk factor." ;
    dmo:name "Hypertension" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "hypertension" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Renin –angiotensin system (RAS) inhibition is recommended for patients with albuminuria and hypertension (HTN)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "These risks are mediated by “indirect” effects such as worsened risk factors (e.g., hyperglycemia, hypertension) as well as by “direct” effects of obesity (e.g., pro-in ﬂammatory state, fat compression of organs)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hypoglycemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The main harm associated with lower HbA1c targets is hypoglycemia." ;
    dmo:name "Hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The main harm associated with lower HbA1c targets is hypoglycemia. In the Action to Control Cardiovascular Risk in Diabetes (ACCORD) trial of T2D, mortality was also higher among participants assigned to the lower HbA1c target, perhaps due to hypoglycemia and related cardiovascular events." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/increased-risk-of-falls> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Increased Risk of Falls" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "CKD patients are at increased risk of falls" ;
    dmo:name "Increased Risk of Falls" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "increased-risk-of-falls" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "However, CKD patients are often older and are at increased risk of falls." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/increased-risk-of-genital-infections> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Increased Risk of Genital Infections" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The Work Group judged that there may be patient-specific factors that would reduce the preference for SGLT2i in specific patients, such as patients at increased risk of volume depletion, genital infections, or lower-limb amputation due to foot ulcerations." ;
    dmo:name "Increased Risk of Genital Infections" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "increased-risk-of-genital-infections" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "patients at increased risk of volume depletion, genital infections, or lower-limb amputation due to foot ulcerations." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/increased-risk-of-lower-limb-amputation-due-to-foot-ulcerations> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Increased Risk of Lower-Limb Amputation Due to Foot Ulcerations" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The Work Group judged that there may be patient-specific factors that would reduce the preference for SGLT2i in specific patients, such as patients at increased risk of volume depletion, genital infections, or lower-limb amputation due to foot ulcerations." ;
    dmo:name "Increased Risk of Lower-Limb Amputation Due to Foot Ulcerations" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "increased-risk-of-lower-limb-amputation-due-to-foot-ulcerations" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "patients at increased risk of volume depletion, genital infections, or lower-limb amputation due to foot ulcerations." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/increased-risk-of-volume-depletion> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Increased Risk of Volume Depletion" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The Work Group judged that there may be patient-specific factors that would reduce the preference for SGLT2i in specific patients, such as patients at increased risk of volume depletion, genital infections, or lower-limb amputation due to foot ulcerations." ;
    dmo:name "Increased Risk of Volume Depletion" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "increased-risk-of-volume-depletion" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "patients at increased risk of volume depletion, genital infections, or lower-limb amputation due to foot ulcerations." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/insulin-use> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Use" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Insulin use is associated with increased risk of hypoglycemia in patients with diabetes and advanced CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Insulin Use" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "insulin-use" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Advanced CKD substantially increases the risk of hypoglycemia in patients with diabetes treated by many oral agents and insulin." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/iron-supplements> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Iron Supplements" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Iron supplements contribute to shortened survival or age of erythrocytes, which lowers HbA1c levels, reducing its reliability as a glycemic marker in advanced CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Iron Supplements" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "iron-supplements" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Conversely, HbA1c is lowered by shortened survival or age of erythrocytes from anemia, transfusions, and use of erythropoiesis-stimulating agents or iron-replacement therapies." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/long-term-metformin-treatment> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Long-term Metformin Treatment" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The reduction in vitamin B12 concentration is increased with increasing duration of metformin therapy." ;
    dmo:name "Long-term Metformin Treatment" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "long-term-metformin-treatment" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "the reduction in vitamin B12 concentration is increased with increasing duration of metformin therapy." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/loss-of-muscle-mass> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Loss of Muscle Mass" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Further, loss of muscle mass and development of complications such as anemia might limit the functional capacity of these patients as kidney function continues to decline." ;
    dmo:name "Loss of Muscle Mass" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "loss-of-muscle-mass" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Further, loss of muscle mass and development of complications such as anemia might limit the functional capacity of these patients as kidney function continues to decline." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/low-physical-activity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Low Physical Activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Patients with diabetes and CKD should be advised to undertake moderate-intensity physical activity for a cumulative duration of at least 150 minutes per week, or to a level compatible with their cardiovascular and physical tolerance." ;
    dmo:name "Low Physical Activity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "low-physical-activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "We recommend that patients with diabetes and CKD be advised to undertake moderate-intensity physical activity for a cumulative duration of at least 150 minutes per week, or to a level compatible with their cardiovascular and physical tolerance (1D)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/metabolic-acidosis> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Metabolic Acidosis" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "A high protein intake could also increase acid load and precipitate or worsen metabolic acidosis, particularly in those with lower levels of kidney function." ;
    dmo:name "Metabolic Acidosis" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "metabolic-acidosis" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A high protein intake could also increase acid load and precipitate or worsen metabolic acidosis, particularly in those with lower levels of kidney function." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/moderately-or-severely-increased-albuminuria> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Moderately or Severely Increased Albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Moderately or severely increased albuminuria is related to increased kidney and cardiovascular risk compared to normal albumin excretion." ;
    dmo:name "Moderately or Severely Increased Albuminuria" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "moderately-or-severely-increased-albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Moderately or severely increased albuminuria is related to increased kidney and cardiovascular risk compared to normal albumin excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/multiple-risk-factors> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Multiple Risk Factors" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Individuals with diabetes and CKD have complex phenotypes including multiple risk factors and complications." ;
    dmo:name "Multiple Risk Factors" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "multiple-risk-factors" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Individuals with diabetes and CKD have complex phenotypes including multiple risk factors and complications." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/nonsteroidal-anti-inflammatory-drug-use> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Nonsteroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drug Use" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是使用RAS阻断剂后血清肌酐急性升高的潜在原因" ;
    dmo:name "Nonsteroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drug Use" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "nonsteroidal-anti-inflammatory-drug-use" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "which often occurs in the setting of volume depletion with aggressive diuretic use and low cardiac output seen in heart failure, or with the use of nonsteroidal anti-in ﬂammatory drugs." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/obesity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Obesity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Obesity is a modifiable risk factor associated with increased risk of progression of CKD and cardiovascular complications in diabetes." ;
    dmo:name "Obesity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "obesity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Smoking cessation WeightExercise" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with diabetes and CKD often have other chronic comorbidities, including obesity, that contribute to the higher risk of CVD and kidney disease progression." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Obesity has numerous adverse health effects, including higher risks of CVD and CKD. These risks are mediated by “indirect” effects such as worsened risk factors (e.g., hyperglycemia, hypertension) as well as by “direct” effects of obesity (e.g., pro-in ﬂammatory state, fat compression of organs)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Overweight, obesity and intentional weight loss in chronic kidney disease: NHANES 1999-2006." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/older-age> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Older Age" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "CKD patients are often older" ;
    dmo:name "Older Age" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "older-age" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "However, CKD patients are often older and are at increased risk of falls." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/overweight> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Overweight" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Overweight is associated with chronic kidney disease based on NHANES 1999-2006 data." ;
    dmo:name "Overweight" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "overweight" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Overweight, obesity and intentional weight loss in chronic kidney disease: NHANES 1999-2006." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/persistent-albuminuria> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Persistent Albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Persistent albuminuria ( >30 mg/g [ >3 mg/mmol]) is associated with increased risk of cardiovascular events." ;
    dmo:name "Persistent Albuminuria" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "persistent-albuminuria" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "d cardiovascular events, as evidenced by persistent albuminuria ( >30 mg/g [ >3 mg/mmol])." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/physical-activity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Physical activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Physical activity is listed as a modifiable risk factor in the holistic approach figure, indicating it is a target for intervention." ;
    dmo:name "Physical activity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "physical-activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Smoking cessationPhysical activity" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/physical-inactivity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Physical Inactivity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Physical activity is listed as a lifestyle factor that contributes to cardiovascular risk, and physical activity is recommended as part of multifactorial intervention." ;
    dmo:name "Physical Inactivity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "physical-inactivity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "lifestyle factors, including diet, smoking, and physical activity." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Smoking cessation WeightExercise" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "tnemeganamthgieWteidyhtlaeH Smoking cessationPhysical activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES) cohort, physical inactivity was associated with increased mortality risk in CKD and non-CKD populations." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Physical inactivity: a risk factor and target for intervention in renal care." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/polypharmacy> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "polypharmacy" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Pre-existing polypharmacy should be considered when choosing interventions to control high potassium levels." ;
    dmo:name "polypharmacy" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "polypharmacy" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For the various interventions to control high potassium, pre-existing polypharmacy, costs, and patient preferences should be considered when choosing among the options." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/poor-glycemic-control> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Poor Glycemic Control" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Poor glycemic control is addressed through first-line therapies like metformin and SGLT2 inhibitors, indicating it is a modifiable risk factor." ;
    dmo:name "Poor Glycemic Control" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "poor-glycemic-control" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Glycemic control is based on insulin for type 1 diabetes (T1D) and a combination of metformin and sodium –glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitors (SGLT2i) for type 2 diabetes (T2D)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/poor-outcomes> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Poor Outcomes" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "These clinical needs call for a change in care delivery in order to stratify risk, triage care, empower patients, and support decision-making in a timely manner." ;
    dmo:name "Poor Outcomes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "poor-outcomes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "These clinical needs call for a change in care delivery in order to stratify risk, triage care, empower patients, and support decision-making in a timely manner." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/pregnancy> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Pregnancy" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "使用ACEi或ARB治疗与胎儿和新生儿不良后果相关" ;
    dmo:name "Pregnancy" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Obstetric" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "pregnancy" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The use of drugs that block the RAS is associated with adverse fetal and neonatal effects, especially with exposure during the second and third trimester." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/reduced-egfr> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Reduced eGFR" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Persistently reduced eGFR (eGFR <60 ml/min per 1.73 m 2) is a defining criterion for CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Reduced eGFR" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "reduced-egfr" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "CKD is de ﬁned as persistently elevated urine albumin excretion ( $30 mg/g [ $3 mg/mmol]), persistently reduced eGFR (eGFR <60 ml/min per 1.73 m 2), or both, for more than 3 months, in accordance with current KDIGO guidelines." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/sarcopenia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Sarcopenia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "In those with CKD, sarcopenia is common and is related to adverse outcomes." ;
    dmo:name "Sarcopenia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "sarcopenia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In those with CKD, sarcopenia is common and is related to adverse outcomes." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/secondhand-smoke-exposure> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Secondhand smoke exposure" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document explicitly states physicians should counsel patients with diabetes and CKD to reduce secondhand smoke exposure." ;
    dmo:name "Secondhand smoke exposure" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "secondhand-smoke-exposure" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Physicians should counsel patients with diabetes and CKD to reduce secondhand smoke exposure." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Recent data also highlight the relationship of secondhand smoke with kidney disease." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/sedentary-behavior> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Sedentary Behavior" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Patients should be advised to avoid sedentary behavior." ;
    dmo:name "Sedentary Behavior" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "sedentary-behavior" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients should be advised to avoid sedentary behavior." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "CKD patients are often sedentary, which is associated with an increased risk of mortality." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "CKD patients are at higher risk of developing sarcopenia, which contributes to adverse outcomes. Resistance training could improve muscle mass; however, there is a lack of data for resistance training in CKD." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/smoking> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Smoking" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Smoking is listed as a modifiable risk factor in the comprehensive management strategy for patients with diabetes and CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Smoking" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "smoking" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Smoking cessation WeightExercise" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Smoking cessationPhysical activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "We recommend advising patients with diabetes and CKD who use tobacco to quit using tobacco products (1D)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "lifestyle factors, including diet, smoking, and physical activity." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "tnemeganamthgieWteidyhtlaeH Smoking cessationPhysical activity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "especially in patients with extensive ASCVD or who are smokers." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/social-disparity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Social Disparity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档中提到在T2D患者中，特别是那些有社会差异的患者，心理社会支持可以改善代谢控制和情绪健康。" ;
    dmo:name "Social Disparity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "SocioDemographic" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "social-disparity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In some patients with T2D, especially those with social disparity or emotional distress, psychosocial support from peers 443 and community healthcare workers444 can also improve metabolic control and emotional well-being, and reduce hospitalizations." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/transfusions> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Transfusions" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Transfusions contribute to shortened survival or age of erythrocytes, which lowers HbA1c levels, reducing its reliability as a glycemic marker in advanced CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Transfusions" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "transfusions" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Conversely, HbA1c is lowered by shortened survival or age of erythrocytes from anemia, transfusions, and use of erythropoiesis-stimulating agents or iron-replacement therapies." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/treatment-with-insulin-or-sulfonylureas> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment with Insulin or Sulfonylureas" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "patients at higher risk for hypoglycemia (e.g., those with low GFR and/or those treated with drugs associated with hypoglycemia, such as insulin or sulfonylureas)." ;
    dmo:name "Treatment with Insulin or Sulfonylureas" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "treatment-with-insulin-or-sulfonylureas" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "those treated with drugs associated with hypoglycemia, such as insulin or sulfonylureas)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/type-1-diabetes> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Type 1 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Type 1 Diabetes is a non-modifiable risk factor for the development of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular complications." ;
    dmo:name "Type 1 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "type-1-diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This guideline focuses on selected topics for which evidence-based guidance can be provided; it does not cover topics like blood pressure and lipid management as these are dealt with in other KDIGO guidelines. However, management of CKD in diabetes requires multifactorial risk factor control, including targeting all of the risk factors mentioned above and also those indicated in Figures 1 and 2." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/type-2-diabetes> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Type 2 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Type 2 Diabetes is a non-modifiable risk factor for the development of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular complications." ;
    dmo:name "Type 2 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "type-2-diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This guideline focuses on selected topics for which evidence-based guidance can be provided; it does not cover topics like blood pressure and lipid management as these are dealt with in other KDIGO guidelines. However, management of CKD in diabetes requires multifactorial risk factor control, including targeting all of the risk factors mentioned above and also those indicated in Figures 1 and 2." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Recently, 2 large clinical trials have examined the cardiovascular and kidney effects of finerenone in those with T2D and albuminuria" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/type-2-diabetes-with-chronic-kidney-disease> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Type 2 Diabetes with Chronic Kidney Disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档中将T2D与CKD的共病状态作为非甾体类MRA推荐的背景，属于不可干预的疾病状态。" ;
    dmo:name "Type 2 Diabetes with Chronic Kidney Disease" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "type-2-diabetes-with-chronic-kidney-disease" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Nonsteroidal MRA have been most rigorously tested in patients with CKD and T2D with residual cardiorenal risk, as evidenced by albuminuria ($30 mg/g [ $3 mg/mmol]) despite treatment with standard of care, including maximal tolerated RAS blockade, and are therefore recommended for this population." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/use-of-certain-oral-glucose-lowering-agents> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Use of Certain Oral Glucose-Lowering Agents" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Certain oral agents are associated with increased risk of hypoglycemia in patients with diabetes and advanced CKD." ;
    dmo:name "Use of Certain Oral Glucose-Lowering Agents" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "use-of-certain-oral-glucose-lowering-agents" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Advanced CKD substantially increases the risk of hypoglycemia in patients with diabetes treated by many oral agents and insulin." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/use-of-concomitant-medications-that-interfere-with-kidney-potassium-excretion> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Use of Concomitant Medications That Interfere With Kidney Potassium Excretion" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "是高钾血症的风险因素，可通过调整药物管理" ;
    dmo:name "Use of Concomitant Medications That Interfere With Kidney Potassium Excretion" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "use-of-concomitant-medications-that-interfere-with-kidney-potassium-excretion" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors for the development of hyperkalemia with the use of drugs that inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "at inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/use-of-glucose-lowering-agents-that-raise-blood-insulin-levels> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Use of Glucose-Lowering Agents That Raise Blood Insulin Levels" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Risk of hypoglycemia is high in patients with advanced CKD who are treated by glucose-lowering agents that raise blood insulin levels (exogenous insulin, sulfonylureas, meglitinides)." ;
    dmo:name "Use of Glucose-Lowering Agents That Raise Blood Insulin Levels" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "use-of-glucose-lowering-agents-that-raise-blood-insulin-levels" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk of hypoglycemia is high in patients with advanced CKD who are treated by glucose-lowering agents that raise blood insulin levels (exogenous insulin, sulfonylureas, meglitinides)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/volume-depletion> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Volume depletion" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document explicitly identifies volume depletion as a risk associated with SGLT2 inhibitor use, particularly in patients with concurrent diuretic use, tenuous volume status, or history of AKI." ;
    dmo:name "Volume depletion" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "volume-depletion" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Volume depletion risk?  Concurrent diuretic use  Tenuous volume status  History of AKI" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors for the development of hyperkalemia with the use of drugs that inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "at inhibit the RAS included CKD, diabetes, decompensated congestive heart failure, volume depletion, advanced age, and use of concomitant medications that interfere with kidney potassium excretion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In the SCORED trial, which also enrolled an exclusively CKD population, diarrhea, genital mycotic infections, volume depletion, and diabetic ketoacidosis were more common with sotagliﬂozin than placebo." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/diarrhea> a dmo:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "Diarrhea" ;
    dmo:name "Diarrhea" ;
    dmo:symptomCode "diarrhea" ;
    dmo:urgency "Routine" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There is risk of adverse gastrointestinal symptoms (nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/nausea> a dmo:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "Nausea" ;
    dmo:hpoCode "HP:0002044" ;
    dmo:name "Nausea" ;
    dmo:symptomCode "nausea" ;
    dmo:urgency "Routine" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "fewer patients in the extended-release group developed nausea during the initial dosing period (2.9%, 3.9%, and 2.4% for the respective extended-release treatment regimens vs. 8.2% in the immediate-release group, P ¼ 0.05)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There is risk of adverse gastrointestinal symptoms (nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/kdigo-2022-clinical-practice-guideline-for-diabetes-management-in-ckd> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/vomiting> a dmo:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "Vomiting" ;
    dmo:name "Vomiting" ;
    dmo:symptomCode "vomiting" ;
    dmo:urgency "Routine" ;
